   105	FR-14. Upsells appear only at relay-needed off-Wi-Fi use, publishing, cloud intent and sharing with Alice. Free local and tailnet routes remain available beside the offer. Preserve exact action drafts; payment cannot publish, launch or grant access by itself.
   106	
   107	FR-15. Checkout is account-owner scoped. Only verified, deduplicated server events activate entitlement; success redirects do not. Existing registered clients refresh a versioned entitlement without re-login. Target activation within ten seconds after webhook confirmation, with pending/retry states and receipts. Owner dogfood uses the planned audited admin step: Accounts → verified Bryan account → Entitlements → Wingthing Pro → Owner grant → Save. There is no shipped owner CLI; build and audit this step before relying on it.
   108	
   109	FR-16. Proposed cancellation stops renewal and retains Pro through the paid period. At effective expiry, close relay/publish/share/SSH paid routes and block cloud starts; stop billable cloud compute according to disclosed terms. Keep local processes and valid LAN/tailnet grants. Retained cloud data/export deadlines and outstanding usage are separately disclosed; deletion cannot be a silent side effect. Payment failure has a distinct dunning deadline, not an invented grace period.
   110	
   111	FR-17. Private publish defaults to owner-only on an exact roost/port/resource ID. Alice authenticates a verified Google/GitHub identity for that resource. Preview access never grants terminal access; observer/controller session roles are separate. Revocation closes active streams and denies future requests. `wt ssh` needs an explicit OS-principal grant and is broader than session control. Do not claim phone relay E2E hides HTTP preview plaintext from a terminating identity gateway.
   112	
   113	### Cloud workspace and lifecycle
   114	
   115	FR-18. Terminal, dashboard and phone can initiate a reviewable cloud draft. The proposed `wt run --cloud <workspace>` syntax is visibly planned. MVP phone initiation uses existing paired-coordinator input against an owner-preauthorized bounded template; no direct VM RPC or new phone account login. Without that template, preserve the draft for Mac approval. Pair cloud-1 independently for direct phone attachment.
   116	
   117	FR-19. A launch review names workspace, repo, branch, agent, model billing mode, allowed secret names, network, region/size, credits, estimate and cap. Reserve account-wide budget atomically before allocation, including concurrent requests, in-flight consumption and a shutdown margin. No charge or VM allocation merely from editing a draft. Idempotent allocation and reconciliation cannot duplicate VMs after a lost response.
   118	
   119	FR-20. Lifecycle includes draft, authorized/reserved, provisioning, booting, agent-starting, ready/running, idle, suspending/stopping, suspended/stopped, resuming, failed, exporting, deleting and deleted, with durable identity and timestamps. “Ready” requires control-plane health and native provider evidence. Failures preserve workspace and receipts and reconcile orphan compute/volumes.
   120	
   121	FR-21. Persistent volume contains repo, edits, project dependencies and chosen artifacts; document exact mount, size, storage billing and retention. Root filesystem/system package persistence is separate. No shared-volume concurrency promise. Snapshot eligibility, cold boot versus memory restore, credential scrubbing, incompatible restore and region migration are explicit, based on VM findings.
   122	
   123	FR-22. GitHub App installations are selected-repo scoped, including private repos. Use short-lived per-repo tokens via a broker; no stored PAT, copied Mac SSH key, token in Git remote URL, image or snapshot. Clone/create branch/push approved branch/open PR under least privilege; no default-branch push by default. Revoke immediately on repo removal, app uninstall or workspace grant loss.
