   138	
   139	FR-32. Use a separate Fly execution organization and per-workspace custom private network; validate provider quotas before launch. Remove the carrier’s internal private-IP authentication fallback and require explicit service credentials. Cloud mode requires functioning cgroup v2 limits instead of silent rlimit fallback. Supervisor/proxy/firewall configuration is outside the unprivileged task’s authority; a guest-root/kernel compromise can bypass guest nftables, so provider-level internet fencing remains a validation gate. Do not grant arbitrary root or claim that local sandbox flexibility already establishes cloud isolation.
