   151	## Non-goals and release sequence
   152	
   153	No public anonymous previews, automatic cross-machine workspace sync, automatic prompt replay, account-wide authority from phone pairing, global zero-knowledge claims, generic SSH shells from phone session grants, indefinite free cloud compute, secret safety via regex alone, team seats/SSO MVP, or release/tag/deploy as part of this storyboard task. No self-hosted Firecracker packing work before validated user demand. Provider-managed sandbox alternatives and later bare-metal margin work belong in the VM recommendation, not the daily-user critical path.
   154	
   155	Release sequence: first make Bryan’s Mac workflow and forge coordinator reliable; then physical-phone local pairing/revoke; recruit first external users and record activation/support evidence; introduce paid relay/private sharing with entitlement; ship a capped BYO-key cloud pilot and measured outcome; expand model billing and teams after demand and security/billing acceptance. [BUILD-PLAN.md](BUILD-PLAN.md) defines executable tasks and release gates.
   156	
   157	## Success metrics
   158	
   159	Metrics below are proposed product targets, not measured results. Gather local consented counters or cohort summaries; do not record transcript, repo names, full paths or credentials. Dogfood and external-user cohorts are separate.
   160	
   161	| Metric | Definition and denominator | Initial target / window |
   162	|---|---|---|
   163	| First-session activation | New installs completing one admitted provider session and a successful detach/reattach within 24h / observable consenting new installs | ≥70% during pilot; report unknown denominator when install telemetry unavailable |
   164	| Time to first useful session | Install-complete to first successful provider interaction, excluding explicit provider-account onboarding and reporting it separately | Median ≤5 minutes, p90 ≤15 minutes |
   165	| Daily-driver reliability | Successful wt claude launches/attaches / explicit attempts; policy denials classified separately | ≥99% across Bryan’s first 100 attempts; zero duplicate unintended launches |
   166	| Multi-machine activation | Users adding forge/another saved machine and successfully attaching once within seven days / users attempting machine add | ≥80%; exact-route and identity failures separately reported |
   167	| Phone activation | Invitation starts reaching confirmed pairing and one read + explicit input + confirmed stop / invitation starts by same physical test device | ≥90% in pilot; zero wrong-wing grants/replays |
   168	| Pro conversion | Free active users subscribing within 30 days of their first contextual paid intent / unique eligible users with that intent | ≥10%; report by four trigger types and net retained conversion after refunds |
   169	| Checkout / entitlement | Completed verified subscriptions / checkout starts; time webhook-confirmed to usable entitled route | ≥60% completion; entitlement p95 ≤10 seconds |
   170	| Cloud activation | First cloud launch reaching ready and a PR/artifact/preview result within seven days / users attempting first paid cloud launch | ≥80%; classify repo, model, capacity and task-quality failures |
   171	| Budget accuracy | Final billed amount within consented cap; duplicated VM allocations, ledger intervals and charges | Zero cap breaches/duplicate charges; estimated vs final delta reported |
   172	| Week-one retention | Activated users using a session on ≥2 distinct days in days 2–7 / activated users observed for seven days | ≥50% in pilot |
   173	| Four-week retention | Activated users with any meaningful session in days 22–28 / activated users with a complete 28-day window | ≥35%; compare phone/Pro/cloud cohorts |
   174	| Paid retention | Pro subscribers renewing into month two / subscribers reaching first renewal, excluding incomplete cohorts | ≥80%; downgrade reasons captured with optional choice |
   175	| Outcomes / support | User-reported useful PR/artifact and resolved blocking support issues / responses and opened blocking issues | Report weekly; median unblock ≤1 business day in staffed pilot |
   176	
   177	Meaningful activity is an admitted provider interaction, confirmed attachment/reading, steering, or explicit stop, not background polling. Retention is cohort-based; don't count incomplete observation windows as churn. Required physical-device security failures block launch regardless of percentage targets. Cost metrics include unit cost, margin, credits, provider invoices and storage/egress, using the VM lane's proposal with measured pilot inputs before expansion.
